    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for Ghost Ride the WHIP is headlined by high-upside offensive environments, with **James Wood** (77.49) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) anchoring our daily production. **James Wood** is our strongest play, benefiting from a high-efficiency matchup against Ritchie (4.93 xERA) and an elite xwOBA profile that justifies the top-tier rating. Similarly, **Tyler Soderstrom** provides significant leverage in the #2 hole, buoyed by a +10% park factor and favorable platoon splits against Montero. **Mickey Moniak** (75.74) and **Brice Turang** (70.78) round out our core; **Mickey Moniak** is particularly intriguing given a +14% dynamic platoon boost and a +14% park factor, though we must monitor the risk posed by the opposing battery\u2019s 55% SB hold rate.\n\nThe decision to bench **Zach McKinstry** (49.14) was the narrowest margin on the board. While **Zach McKinstry** offered potential SB upside\u2014a category we consistently overweight\u2014he was squeezed out by the sheer efficiency of **Brice Turang** at the leadoff spot and the high-ceiling matchup for **Mickey Moniak**. We are also keeping a close eye on the weather and external factors; **Jose Caballero** (52.02) faces a stiff wind-in caveat that depressed his output, and **Corbin Carroll** (59.15) must navigate the defensive prowess of the opposition\u2019s elite 1.86s pop-time catcher, which complicates his aggressive base-running game plan. \n\nWhile we are optimized for total offensive output, we remain cautious regarding the G. Williams (2.99 xERA) start against **Gabriel Moreno** (46.11) and **Corbin Carroll**, as his elite skill set creates a significant floor risk. We continue to hold **Vinnie Pasquantino** on the IL while awaiting his return to bolster our power metrics, and we will keep **Austin Riley**, **Cole Young**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Max Muncy**, and **Edwin Arroyo** in reserve to capitalize on future favorable park shifts or injury-induced lineup adjustments.",
